## 席位核对

**L1 first review (full) · REWORK, paper only** · Head-sha: `1074c040a7c1686fadeebe2e9874979747f1de05` · card #34655 half A (`Fixes #34655`) · read 2026-11-17T13:16Z

There is no earlier L1 record. The contract review passed twice: 6946901031 at `bef53a47`, then 6947617913 at `5fe7b810` with S3 open. Inputs:
- half-A claim 6946117692 and amendments 6943849177, 6944001902 and 6944184550;
- hand-off 6948282082 and takeover 6948719649;
- the PR body;
- the net diff from merge-base `c4c0794d` (27 files, +1120 / -28), with the delta `5fe7b810..1074c040` read line by line;
- check-runs on this head.

One finding, and it is paper. The code reads correct.

### Must-fix

**M1. Six paths fall outside half A's claimed surface, and the card has no amendment for them.** Amendments 6944001902 and 6944184550 name:
- `flow.zod.ts`, `flow-activation-projection.ts`, `engine.ts`, `flow-clone.ts` and `package-unmanaged-install.ts`;
- the ADR-0126 note, the automation skill and the generated spec artefacts;
- tests beside those files, and `.changeset/`;
- in `flow-definitions.ts`, `hydrateFlowActivations` only.

The diff also moves these:
- `packages/services/service-automation/src/flow-registration-checks.ts` (the refusal joins the one check list, which is the L2 S1 fix);
- `packages/services/service-automation/src/plugin.ts` and `src/index.ts` (`packagedFlowDefaultReader` and the `PackagedFlowDefaultSource` type export, the L2 S2 fix);
- `scripts/check-skills-token-ratchet.mjs` (the automation skill's ceiling 6903 → 6992, with its arithmetic);
- `packages/spec/src/system/metadata-form-zod-reconciliation.test.ts` and `packages/metadata-protocol/src/protocol.meta-types-degenerate-derivation.test.ts` (existing tests forced by the new key, the same pair #34719's amendment named).

Each one is forced by an L2 fix, by the new key or by a gate. Please post one amendment on #34655 that names them with these reasons. The card thread is gone, so area o3-J posts it. A delta ACCEPT on this same head follows.

### Delta `5fe7b810..1074c040` (the L2 6947617913 items)

- **S3 is closed.** `refuseUnpackagedDefaultActive` now asks `isShippedFlowName`: any package's loader set holding the name, not "one owner". It asks `packagedFlowSlotOwner` of each candidate package: the slots holding the bare name now, plus the body's own `_packageId`, which is used only to pick which package to ask. A stamp naming a package that ships no such flow therefore answers no. It is pinned by the new describe "(L2 S3) — a name two packages hold keeps the key" in `flow-default-active-34655.test.ts`: two holders, a re-sync, a third holder.
- **N8 is closed.** The changeset now names `AutomationEngine.setPackagedFlowDefaultSource` and `PackagedFlowDefaultSource` as public API. It states the fail-open of an engine composed without a reader, and why. The integration test now reads the package's body through the real protocol (`packagedFlowDefaultReader` with no mock), with the pair CONTROL answering `undefined`.
- **N9 is closed.** `packagedFlowDefault` caches the reader's answer per armed body (`WeakMap`, reset whenever either reader is attached), so `isFlowEnabled` no longer calls the loader set on every read. The loader-armed path still reads `armed.defaultActive` directly. The cache relies on each re-sync re-registering a freshly parsed body, as its docblock states. Recorded here for the seat's L2 delta, not as a finding.
- **N10 and N11** are body and jsdoc text, and they now read correctly.

### Checklist (the rest holds)

- **Shape:** Draft against `main`. The only closing keyword is `Fixes #34655`: half A closes the card, and half B (#34810) only `Refs` it. The body's signed trailer is seat 3's now, and the withdrawn `Contract-review-handoff` line is gone.
- **Declarations:** `Clause-②: yes (widening)` matches the diff. `FlowSchema.defaultActive` is a new optional key on a `strictObject`, so a flow declaring it was refused before. An environment-authored flow is still refused, now with a sentence. Nothing that registered before is refused. `Metadata-protocol: added` is right. The changeset levels are spec and service-automation `minor`, runtime and metadata-protocol `patch`, and they name every published package whose `src` moved. The `skills/**` text ships in `@objectstack/skills`, which is in the same `fixed` group.
- **Seat rulings (6944001902) are kept:**
  - the key is `defaultActive`, absent means on;
  - the default is read at the consult point and never seeded as a row;
  - the administrator's row wins;
  - an override never changes the package's default (`packagedFlowDefault` reads the package's own body);
  - the ADR-0126 §4 amendment note is in this PR.
- **The ADR note against the code:**
  - an "on" row counts only for the package that holds the flow now;
  - `hydrateFlowActivations` arms a switched-on flow through `activateFlowTrigger`, whose gate still declines a flow its status disarms;
  - a clone drops the key (`FLOW_CLONE_DROPPED_KEYS`);
  - an unmanaged install copies `false` as `status: 'obsolete'` (`copyUnmanagedFlowSwitch`), keeping an `obsolete`/`invalid` status that is already there.
  Each claim matches its named symbol.
- **Docs made false:** none found. The `FlowSchema.defaultActive` describe, the regenerated `references/automation/flow.mdx` and `references/api/automation-api.mdx`, and the changeset agree with the engine. The half B interplay holds: switching on a `status: 'active', defaultActive: false` flow is not refused by #34810's status check, and `obsolete` still is.
- **Skills (`skills/**`, whole-pack read):** one 5-line paragraph in `objectstack-automation/SKILL.md`. It points at the switch the paragraph before it introduces instead of restating it, so it adds no duplicate teaching to the pack. Eval 24 asks the real authoring question, and its `must_contain` tokens (`defaultActive: false`, `toggle`) are words a correct reply carries. The ratchet moves +89, which is the measured addition only.
- **Tests:** `flow-default-active-34655.test.ts` (new) covers ships-off, the switch on and off, restart and upgrade, override, two holders, the refusal and the dry run. There are also new spec, runtime-clone and unmanaged-install pins, and the integration test reads through the real protocol.
- **Gates at this head:** latest attempt per check, 86 runs: `success` or `skipped`, none failed. `Test Core (2/10)`, red on its first attempt (`anchor.test.ts` hook timeout under load, unrelated), is `success` on its rerun, and so is the `Test Core` roll-up. `PR-body guards`, red at the claim-line parse, is `success` after the body edit.

### Owed after this (nothing here readies, queues or arms the PR)

- The area posts the claim amendment (M1). A delta ACCEPT on this head follows.
- **Seat L2 delta at `CONTRACT_REVIEW_TIER`** on `5fe7b810..1074c040`: the faces are a new spec key and governed `docs/adr` + `skills/**`. The reviewer closes S3 and N8–N11.
- **Tier H:** governed (`packages/spec/src`, `docs/adr`), so os-zhuang must approve on the final head. It lands after #34654 and #34810 (half B is in a fix round now), merging `main` after each.
